WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.635
-Hi, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.137
Thank you so much
for watching.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.738
It is Thursday, which basically
means it's Friday, really.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:08.607
Right? So we made it through
another week.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:11.710
I'm so happy to anyone that's
home and staying safe

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:13.145
and wearing the masks,

00:00:13.145 --> 00:00:18.251
and to anyone who is suffering
with this awful pandemic,

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.821
I wish you a speedy,
speedy recovery.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.556
I'm going to try to make you
laugh right now.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.991
Here are some jokes.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.726
Let's get to some news, guys.

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.028
As the coronavirus continues
to spread across the country,

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:32.132
a new poll finds that
if cases keep spiking,

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:36.636
65% of Americans support
returning to lockdown.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:42.808
First off, what do you mean
returning to lockdown?

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:44.376
I haven't left.

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:48.414
My hair looks like a wig.
What...

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:49.949
You know your country's
doing well

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.784
when shutting everything down
is polling higher

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:55.254
than both
presidential candidates.

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.690
Yep, people support another
lockdown, especially after

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.426
they got 35 "save the dates"

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.393
for all the weddings
that got moved.

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:03.162
They're like...

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.131
"Ah, this lockdown,
I don't...

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.600
I'm happy for you guys."

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.071
76% of Americans over 55
support returning to lockdown.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.440
They said they finally
figured out how to use Netflix

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.742
and they're not
stopping now.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.744
Said, "Don't make me leave.
Really?"

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:21.414
By the way, my dad's watched
everything.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.751
I think he thinks the one screen
is everything on Netflix.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.552
So, I'm like, great.
So he does that.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.321
He's done TVs, movies.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.956
I haven't even told him
what search does.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.991
-Don't.
-No, it's great.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.226
He's happy.

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:36.429
That's right. The coronavirus
is affecting everyone,

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.531
even those close to
the president.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:41.835
-Dozens of Secret Service agents
are being told to quarantine

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.736
after working at
President Trump's rally

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:47.606
in Tulsa, Oklahoma,
where a huge swath of people

00:01:47.606 --> 00:01:49.208
did not wear masks.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.844
-Seriously, you know
we're in crazy times

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:52.645
when the Secret Service
needs protection

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.648
from the president.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.483
If you are worried about
Trump's safety, don't.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.751
He's fine.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.086
While the agents are
quarantined,

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.255
Trump will be guarded
by Eric and Don Jr.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.858
using a pair of
SpongeBob walkie-talkies.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.627
[ Imitates static ]
"Can you hear me?"

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:11.430
[ Imitates static ]
"Yeah. I'm right next to you."

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.899
[ Imitates static ]
"Okay."

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.802
Well, a lot of people are
blaming the Trump administration

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:18.371
for mishandling the virus.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.873
But not everything has gone
wrong, right?

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:22.775 line:0%
-A startling new report
out today

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.244 line:0%
that more than 1 million
dead Americans got

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:29.682 line:0%
those pandemic stimulus checks
totaling $1.4 billion.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.386
-I pay dead people.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.522
Even dead people were like,

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:39.025
Only 1,200 bucks
for three months?

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:42.161
Thanks, I guess."

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:44.931
That's a tough gaffe for Trump
in what otherwise has been

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.366
a flawless year.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.101
Wouldn't you agree?

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:51.804
Yep, 1 million dead people
received checks.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:56.509
Even people investing in Quibi
think that's a waste of money.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.444
Trump was like,
"It will all be worth it

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:02.081
when they head to the polls
in November."

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.116
Actually, Trump was furious
about the mistake

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:05.918
and asked that all
the dead people immediately

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:09.121
send their checks back.

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:11.023
As if things weren't bad enough,
I read that

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:12.825
a bunch of hand sanitizers
were just recalled

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:16.562
for containing lethal toxins.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.230
That's insane.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.066
I've been using so much hand
sanitizer these days.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:23.703
Anyways, one of these companies
just put out a new ad.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.037
Check it out.

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:27.607
-For years, Cleansior
Hand Sanitizer has been

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.909
one of the most trusted names
in clean.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.911
And now with the coronavirus
pandemic,

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.680
hand sanitizer is more
important than ever.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.783
But maybe you heard that our
product contains toxic methanol.

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.886
Whoops.
Yeah, that's on us.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:43.422
Luckily, you can continue to use
our hand sanitizer worry free,

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:46.559
with our new Cleansior
Hand Sanitizer Sanitizer.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.295
Our Hand Sanitizer Sanitizer
is the first hand sanitizer

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:51.464
that sanitizes your
hand sanitized hands

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.632
to keep them
hand sanitizer free.

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:56.502
Simply use our hand sanitizer
as normal, keeping in mind

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.504
that exposure to methanol
can lead to nausea, vomiting,

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.407
blurred vision or death, then
wash away the hand sanitizer

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.475
with our sanitizer sanitizer

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:05.477
before your nervous system
totally shuts down.

00:04:05.477 --> 00:04:07.613
Ha-ha! So easy.

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:09.882
It will almost be like
we didn't try to kill you

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.117
with something that's supposed
to keep you safe.

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:13.986
When you're done, just throw
both bottles

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:15.922
into a hazardous waste
container, burn it,

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.857
and then throw the ashes
in the ocean -- ta-da!

00:04:18.857 --> 00:04:21.193
Cleansior Hand Sanitizer
Sanitizer.

00:04:21.193 --> 00:04:24.364
Keep sanitizing until
all the sanitizer is sanitized!

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.434
-Just ordered it on Amazon.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.802
[ Clears throat ]

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.837
Well, this is going viral down
in Palm Beach, Florida.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:35.408
They held a town hall to talk
about a new mask mandate.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.410
A lot of people showed up
to speak against it,

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:42.081
and what they said was pretty --
well, just watch.

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.383 line:0%
-You literally cannot
mandate somebody

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.487 line:0%
to wear a mask knowing that
that mask is killing people.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:51.256 line:0%
Every single one of you that are
obeying the devil's laws

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:53.025 line:0%
are going to be arrested.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:54.927 line:0%
-Keep taking the road
of least resistance.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:58.364 line:0%
Keep listening to the TV
brainwashing you from birth.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.666 line:0%
-And they want
to throw God's

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:03.870 line:0%
wonderful breathing system
out the door.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.305 line:0%
You are all turning your backs
on it.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.541 line:0%
-Doctor, I really have
many question marks

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:11.077 line:0%
about your degrees and
what you really know.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:13.913 line:0%
And I would ask suggestively
that you go back to school

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:16.815 line:0%
and get educated.
-Ma'am --

00:05:16.815 --> 00:05:19.819
-If you think that's upsetting,
Trump just put them in charge

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:23.856
of the coronavirus
task force, so...

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:26.124
That's right. Not only
is the clip viral,

00:05:26.124 --> 00:05:29.228
but so are the people.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:32.698
That was like a dramatic reading
of your uncle's Facebook posts.

00:05:32.698 --> 00:05:38.837
[ Laughing ]

00:05:38.837 --> 00:05:40.840
This one I like.
This is the one.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.474
Um...
[ Clears throat ]

00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:44.243
Finally, city officials
were like,

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.745
"Are you here for
Bath Salts Anonymous?

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:48.981
Because that's down the hall.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:53.252
[ Laughing ]

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.321
Bath Salts Anonymous,
come on.

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.422
That's not a real thing.

00:05:57.422 --> 00:05:59.859
If you want to meet these people
in person, I should add

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.293
they'll be signing autographs

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.830
at a recently pulled down
5G tower.

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.867
[ Laughs ]

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.869
Afterward, Florida officials
were like,

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:12.171
"That was actually one of
our better meetings,

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.706
don't you think?"

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.511
Well, it's been a few days
since New York started

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:21.380
Phase 2 of reopening,
and people are excited

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.883
that outdoor dining
is allowed.

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.484
Yeah. Streets and sidewalks
are filled

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.887
with tables and chairs,
and people are already leaving

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.956
Yelp reviews
about their experiences.

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:31.757
Take a look.
This one says,

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.626
"The baked chicken was
very juicy.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:35.494
Probably because someone's
window air conditioner

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:36.963
was dripping on it."

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.765
This next one says,
"Great service,

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:40.466
but it was hard to hear
the specials

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.901
over all the illegal fireworks."

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:44.903
This one says,
"It's always been my dream

00:06:44.903 --> 00:06:47.907
to dine al fresco at
the Penn Station Hooters."

00:06:49.107 --> 00:06:52.044
[ Laughs ]

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.646
Al fresco.

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:56.315
[ Laughing ]

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.851
[ Ding ]

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:01.154
This next one says,
"There was a hair in my food,

00:07:01.154 --> 00:07:02.654
but it was mine
because I haven't gotten

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:05.057
a haircut since February!"

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:10.196
This next one says,
"A very short wait,

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:13.699
but the only thing on the menu
was leftover banana bread."

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:16.802
I get that.
Lastly, this one says,

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:19.204
"Risking my life was so worth
two Coors Lights

00:07:19.204 --> 00:07:21.406
and a plate
of jalapeño poppers."

00:07:21.406 --> 00:07:24.310
And finally, guys, there's a lot
of uncertainty about sports,

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:27.279
but there is one event
that is coming back.

00:07:27.279 --> 00:07:31.049
-The 146th Kentucky Derby
will be held on September 5th,

00:07:31.049 --> 00:07:32.585
and spectators will be allowed,

00:07:32.585 --> 00:07:34.653
according to
the Churchill Downs Racetrack.

00:07:34.653 --> 00:07:36.655
-For fans, it will be
the most exciting two minutes

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:38.090
in sports, followed by

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.893
the most boring two weeks
in quarantine.

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:42.795
In the midst of this
challenging year though,

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.363
I think it will be kind of fun

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.798
to watch a man
in a seersucker suit

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:49.768
throw up a mint julep,
don't you think?

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:51.937
Organizers say, though,
that they'll take

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:54.006
every safety precaution

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:56.008
before strapping
an 80-pound man

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:59.312
to a horse running
40 miles per hour.

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:00.613
Okay?

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:05.451
[ Chuckles ]
Wait, that doesn't sound --

00:08:05.451 --> 00:08:07.519
I know.

00:08:07.519 --> 00:08:09.688
It's not you, is it?

00:08:09.688 --> 00:08:11.090
Let 'em do it.

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:14.493
Oh, here's the last one.

00:08:14.493 --> 00:08:16.162
The good news is

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:17.963
the hats are big enough
that they automatically

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:19.731
make you social distance.

00:08:19.731 --> 00:08:21.000
Ha-ha! There you go.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.702
All right, everybody,
that is my monologue.

